{"seq": 93, "t": 312.818, "kind": "message", "agent": "agent1", "to": "agent2", "chars": 2312, "content": "agent1: agreed, I own first/last text. Compiled + tests pass (hello/''/--foo/foo-- with default and strip). Paste this VERBATIM in place of the current first() and last() (incl. doc comments; blank line after last's closing brace; keep default: Option<Str>, returns StrResult<Str>, NOT Value). Note: use set.as_str().contains(c) since Str has an inherent contains(StrPattern) that shadows str::contains.\n    /// Extracts the first grapheme cluster of the string. Returns the default\n    /// value if the string is empty or fails with an error if no default value\n    /// was specified.\n    #[func]\n    pub fn first(\n        &self,\n        /// A default value to return if the string is empty.\n        #[named]\n        default: Option<Str>,\n        /// A set of characters to remove from the start of the string before\n        /// extracting the grapheme cluster.\n        #[named]\n        strip: Option<Str>,\n    ) -> StrResult<Str> {\n        let text: &str = match &strip {\n            Some(set) if !set.is_empty() => {\n                self.0.trim_start_matches(|c: char| set.as_str().contains(c))\n            }\n            _ => self.0.as_str(),\n        };\n        text.graphemes(true)\n            .next()\n            .map(Into::into)\n            .or(default)\n            .ok_or_else(string_is_empty)\n    }\n\n    /// Extracts the last grapheme cluster of the string. Returns the default\n    /// value if the string is empty or fails with an error if no default value\n    /// was specified.\n    #[func]\n    pub fn last(\n        &self,\n        /// A default value to return if the string is empty.\n        #[named]\n        default: Option<Str>,\n        /// A set of characters to remove from the end of the string before\n        /// extracting the grapheme cluster.\n        #[named]\n        strip: Option<Str>,\n    ) -> StrResult<Str> {\n        let text: &str = match &strip {\n            Some(set) if !set.is_empty() => {\n                self.0.trim_end_matches(|c: char| set.as_str().contains(c))\n            }\n            _ => self.0.as_str(),\n        };\n        text.graphemes(true)\n            .next_back()\n            .map(Into::into)\n            .or(default)\n            .ok_or_else(string_is_empty)\n    }\nI will not change anything else in str.rs. Tests (not in patch): tests/suite/foundations/str.typ only.", "timestamp": 1792163121.1441755, "timestamp_iso": "2026-10-16T15:05:21.144178", "message_id": 93, "send_id": 92}
